# E00 Agents3: parallel, so the agents interleave and the monitor may handle a "done" in the turn it is sent or in the
# next one; compared: the lines of the monitor in order (three rounds of 4 sends and 4 "done"), the lines of each agent
# in order, who is addressed, and the turn reports. The monitor addresses the agents in the order of the environment,
# which differs from the C# (ISO e): names are compared as multisets.
ignore ^$
cover all
fact monitor ^(?:monitor: start round (\d) in (setup|act)|-> (sending) to agent\d|\t\[agent\d -> monitor\]: (done))$
fact agent ^\t\[monitor -> (agent\d)\]: (start|continue)$
fact sendto ^-> sending to (agent\d)$
fact done ^\t\[(agent\d) -> monitor\]: done$
fact environment ^(Turn \d+ finished|Simulation finished)$
same monitor seq
same agent seq by 0
same sendto bag
same done bag
same environment seq
check monitor count == 27
check agent count == 12
fact error (Exception|out of range)
optional error
check error count == 0
